# PX4 parameters for the real aircraft: indoor Vicon lab, GPS-denied, safety pilot on RC.
# Vicon aids EKF2 only while the loop does NOT have the aircraft (vicon_px4_bridge,
# aiding_policy:=gated), so the scored window is still unaided. See RUNNING_HW.md.
# QGC format: <sysid> <compid> <name> <value> <type>; type 6 = INT32, 9 = REAL32.
# NOT derived from the SITL airframe, which a real FC cannot load and which disables failsafes.
# Every failsafe action below must name a POSITION-FREE mode: PX4 dead-reckons a local position
# that is kilometres wrong indoors, and will act on it.

# No GNSS aiding at all (7 is PX4's default bitmask).
1	1	EKF2_GPS_CTRL	0	6
# Barometric height. Deliberately NOT 3 (Vision): the Vicon stream is cut at the handover, and
# the height reference must not vanish at 1.2 m. Horizontal and yaw are the only EV contributions.
1	1	EKF2_HGT_REF	0	6

# --- Vicon external vision ------------------------------------------------------------------
# bit0 horizontal position ONLY. Vertical (bit1) is off so the cut at the handover cannot remove
# the height reference; velocity (bit2) is off because a differentiated mocap velocity is noise
# EKF2 cannot gate.
#
# Yaw (bit3, which would make this 9) is deliberately NOT fused. Fusing it makes EKF2's heading
# datum whatever the Vicon frame says, so a frame error becomes unfalsifiable from inside the
# estimator - a self-consistent wrong frame re-anchors the filter and reports zero innovation.
# With yaw off, EKF2's magnetometer heading stays an INDEPENDENT witness, which is exactly what
# vicon_px4_bridge's frame check compares against before it will publish anything. 9 is only safe
# once the Vicon datum has been measured against magnetic north on site.
#
# EKF2 stops EV fusion 400 ms after the last sample (2 x EV_MAX_INTERVAL), which is how
# vicon_px4_bridge cuts aiding without touching a parameter in flight.
1	1	EKF2_EV_CTRL	1	6
# 1 = take the noise from the parameters below. The bridge reports a fixed variance, so there is
# nothing better in the message.
1	1	EKF2_EV_NOISE_MD	1	6
# Vicon is millimetric; 2 cm is deliberately conservative, and it is a LOWER bound on trust.
1	1	EKF2_EVP_NOISE	0.02	9
# Inert while EKF2_EV_CTRL is 1 (no attitude fusion); kept so the yaw arm needs no new value.
1	1	EKF2_EVA_NOISE	0.05	9
# TODO BEFORE FLIGHT: the Vicon marker centroid relative to the CoG, metres, body FRD.
1	1	EKF2_EV_POS_X	0.0	9
1	1	EKF2_EV_POS_Y	0.0	9
1	1	EKF2_EV_POS_Z	0.0	9
# TODO BEFORE FLIGHT: set from the bridge's reported age mean. REBOOT REQUIRED to take effect.
1	1	EKF2_EV_DELAY	0.0	9
# PX4's default. The SITL airframe's 0.0 disables the mag-heading observability guard.
1	1	EKF2_MAG_ACCLIM	0.5	9

# TODO BEFORE FLIGHT: the lab's declination. Without GNSS nothing supplies it, and the default
# is silently zero. DECL_TYPE 6 clears bit 0 so MAG_DECL is used. Moot WHILE Vicon is aiding -
# EV yaw makes the heading relative to the Vicon frame, not True North - but it binds again after
# the cut, when the heading dead-reckons from the Vicon datum.
#1	1	EKF2_DECL_TYPE	6	6
#1	1	EKF2_MAG_DECL	0.0	9

# The Pi's XRCE-DDS link. TODO BEFORE FLIGHT: confirm the Pi's UART is wired to TELEM2.
1	1	UXRCE_DDS_CFG	102	6
1	1	SER_TEL2_BAUD	921600	6

# RC only. The safety pilot is on a transmitter, not on DDS.
1	1	COM_RC_IN_MODE	0	6
# PX4's default, set deliberately - and it must NEVER be the SITL value (-1, override disabled).
# Any stick movement while the loop owns the aircraft hands it back, and indoors it never returns:
# commander reassigns the mode intent to POSCTL unconditionally. The trap is wider than OFFBOARD -
# during a lock-loss failsafe nav_state is already Altitude while the intent is still OFFBOARD, and
# a correction there is still an override. The pilot lets go after granting consent, and stays off
# through a transient failsafe unless taking the aircraft for good.
1	1	MAN_OVERRIDE_SPD	1.0	9

# Offboard loss -> Altitude. Default 0 (Position) and 5 (Hold) both need horizontal position.
# Gated aiding makes 5 (Hold) tempting, because Vicon returns the moment OFFBOARD is lost - but
# EKF2 needs at least 400 ms to re-acquire, and Hold on a momentarily-bad position is worse than
# Altitude. Revisit only once the resume latency has been measured in the lab.
1	1	COM_OBL_RC_ACT	1	6
# With the bridge's 0.3 s setpoint timeout this is the 1.3 s authority gap.
1	1	COM_OF_LOSS_T	1.0	9
# RC loss -> Land. Default 2 is Return, which needs a home position.
1	1	NAV_RCL_ACT	3	6
# Datalink loss disabled; the ground station is not in the control path.
1	1	NAV_DLL_ACT	0	6
# No exceptions: bit 2 would exempt offboard from the RC-loss failsafe.
1	1	COM_RCL_EXCEPT	0	6
# Geofence off. Default 2 is Hold, reachable indoors via the baro-only vertical fence.
1	1	GF_ACTION	0	6
# Warning only; the pilot is on the sticks.
1	1	COM_ACT_FAIL_ACT	0	6
# Warning only; 3 and 4 both Return, which is unavailable here.
1	1	COM_LOW_BAT_ACT	0	6

# The aircraft flies a 3S pack (T5000 3S).
1	1	BAT1_N_CELLS	3	6

# TODO BEFORE FLIGHT: measure on a real hover, and pass the same number as hover_thrust:=.
# SITL derives 0.69 for 3S at the 1.30 kg parts-list mass; a reading far from that means the mass is off.
1	1	MPC_THR_HOVER	0.60	9

# MC_*RATE_* are deliberately absent. The SITL gains were tuned against Gazebo's rotor model;
# start from the PX4 F450 defaults or autotune, then record the result here.

# From boot until disarm. Start-up failures never arm, so the default 0 logs nothing.
1	1	SDLOG_MODE	1	6

# TODO BEFORE FLIGHT, with the pilot at the transmitter; the channel numbers are placeholders.
# Consent: map the handover switch to AUX1, then launch consent_rc_aux:=1. Unmapped reads as no consent.
#1	1	RC_MAP_AUX1	7	6
# Mode slots: 8 Stabilized or 1 Altitude only. Position (2) parks PX4's intended mode at POSCTL
# when it cannot run, locking the loop out of OFFBOARD.
#
# PILOT-BRIEF DECISION, not yet taken: under gated aiding POSCTL *can* run, because Vicon is
# feeding EKF2 whenever the loop does not have the aircraft. A Position slot would then be a real
# safety gain - Altitude has no horizontal hold at all, which is the condition that drifted 300 m.
# It is only safe because commanding OFFBOARD sets the intent to OFFBOARD, and because the pilot
# is already briefed to let go of the sticks. Enable it deliberately, with the pilot, or not at all.
#1	1	COM_FLTMODE2	2	6
#1	1	RC_MAP_FLTMODE	5	6
#1	1	COM_FLTMODE1	8	6
#1	1	COM_FLTMODE4	1	6
#1	1	COM_FLTMODE6	1	6
# Kill switch.
#1	1	RC_MAP_KILL_SW	6	6
